course: dictionary
lesson: 6545
title: Newfoundland: an island and a dog
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «John Cabot reached Newfoundland in 1497» is about a place, because reached and sailed are clues about travel. «A Newfoundland dog» is about an animal, because dog comes right after the word.
explain: Look for clue words near the name. Words like island, Canada, fishing or icebergs point to the place. Words like dog, coat, rescue or swimming point to the animal. «Labradors and Newfoundlands are water rescue dogs» is about dogs, because of rescue and swimming.
explain: Use the swap test to check. Put island or dog in place of the word and see if the sentence still makes sense. «Around Newfoundland so many cod were caught» works with island. «A Newfoundland can tow a small boat» works with dog. If the clues are still unclear, check a dictionary.
fact: Newfoundland is a large island off the east coast of Canada.
fact: Newfoundland and Labrador is a Canadian province, made of the island and the mainland area of Labrador.
fact: A Newfoundland is a very large, strong, gentle dog with a thick coat.
fact: Newfoundland dogs are famous for rescuing people from water.
fact: Nana in «Peter Pan» was a Newfoundland dog.
exercise: «John Cabot reached Newfoundland in 1497.» What is Newfoundland in this sentence? | A very strong, gentle dog | *A large island off the east coast of Canada | A city in Italy | A kind of Viking boat
exercise: «A Newfoundland can tow a small boat.» What is a Newfoundland in this sentence? | *A very large, strong, gentle dog | A Canadian province | A helicopter | An island off Canada
exercise: Which clue in «a Newfoundland dog» shows that the word means the animal? | *Dog | Canada | Island | Newfoundland
test: «Around Newfoundland so many cod were caught that fishing was closed in 1992.» What does Newfoundland mean here? | A gentle dog with a thick coat | A type of fish | A ship's captain | *The island off the east coast of Canada
test: «Newfoundlands have webbed toes and strong swimming muscles.» What does Newfoundlands mean here? | *The dogs | The island | The Canadian province | The Vikings
exam: «Newfoundland is famous for icebergs and puffins.» Which swap test shows that the word means the place? | *Put in island, and the sentence still makes sense | Put in sad, and the sentence still makes sense | Put in dog, and the sentence still makes sense | Put in Nana, and the sentence still makes sense
